      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have observed the same behaviour when teleporting the player in every FixedUpdate() in combination with forward movement input. Depending on the running speed I had set in the VrcPlayerApi the avatar could outrun the camera and would snap back around once a second.\nIn U# (FixedUpdate()):\n`localPlayer.TeleportTo(playerPosition, playerRotation, VRC_SceneDescriptor.SpawnOrientation.AlignPlayerWithSpawnPoint, true);`",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-05-21T17:13:33.526Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There seems to be issues with code that deals with moving the players position from one location to another, following very simple code in the images provided. I have a trigger object that you can click on that sends you to another location through an empty with the code in the bottom half. However here is the issue: It moves the players camera, not the avatar. There is rare occasions where it works as intended however for a large portion of attempts it leaves you with an \"out of body experience\". A link to the world available: https://vrchat.com/i/boy-chaniwonk-f96a1 --- Update: After uploading to server and attempting in VR, it seems to work as intended more consistently thus could be a desktop only issue",
